cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The Airy edge of shear hydrodynamics: a large-d law for the critical point of the AdS_{d+1} black brane, with a numerical radius bound at d = 512, 1024 and 8192"
authors:
  - name: "Moki&Julio"
date-released: 2026-11-04
version: "1.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Hashirama1337s/airy-edge-hydrodynamics"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - large D
  - holography
  - hydrodynamics
  - radius of convergence
  - quasinormal modes
  - Airy function
abstract: >-
  Large-d law for the critical point that limits shear hydrodynamics of the AdS black brane: approach to (-2, i) as
  d^(-1/3) with a coefficient from the first zero of Ai'^2 - U Ai^2 (formal matched asymptotics), a no-fit forward test
  at d = 8192-32768, and a numerical radius bound at d = 512, 1024 and 8192. Data, code and sealed-test records included.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "The Gregory-Laflamme threshold to order 1/n^12 and its resummation to AdS screening masses"
    authors:
      - name: "Moki&Julio"
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23940227"
